course: dictionary
lesson: 14354
title: Omens: signs of what is to come
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An omen is a sign or event that some people believe shows what will happen in the future. «The crow landed on the roof and let out a loud cry, a bad omen, the old farmer said.» The word sign tells you the crow is a clue, and the words what will happen tell you the trouble is still to come.
explain: Omens can be good or bad. «Seeing a rainbow after the storm felt like a good omen.» The words good and bad before omen tell you which kind it is. Phrases such as «an omen of» help too: «Dark clouds gathered over the castle, an omen of trouble to come.»
explain: Writers use omens to build suspense, so readers wonder what will happen next. Ask yourself: is this sign a clue about the future? Then check the words around omen to see whether it is good or bad.
fact: An omen is a sign or event that some people believe shows what will happen in the future.
fact: Omens can be good, as in «a good omen», or bad, as in «a bad omen».
fact: Phrases to look for are «a good omen», «a bad omen» and «an omen of».
fact: Science and most people today see omens as superstition, not as real proof of the future.
fact: Omens are common in myths, history and stories, where they help to build suspense.
exercise: «The black cat crossed the path in front of him, an omen of bad luck, some said.» What is an omen? | A very old castle | A loud noise in the night | A kind of cat | *A sign that some people believe shows what will happen in the future
exercise: «Seeing a rainbow after the storm felt like a good omen.» What does the word good tell you? | The storm has ended forever | *The sign shows that something good will happen in the future | The rainbow is made of water | The children were happy
exercise: «Dark clouds gathered over the castle, an omen of trouble to come.» Find and copy the word that shows the trouble is still in the future. | *to come | gathered | castle | Dark
test: Some people believe a broken mirror is an omen. What does omen mean here? | A piece of glass that is broken | A happy party | *A sign of what might happen in the future | A kind of mirror
test: «The comet blazed across the sky before the battle, an omen the soldiers feared.» What did the soldiers believe? | *The comet showed that something would happen in the future | The comet was a star that would fall to Earth | The comet was only a bright light with no meaning | The comet was a sign that a good meal was coming
exam: What is one reason writers use omens in stories? | *To build suspense and make readers wonder what will happen next | To make the story shorter | Because omens are proof that magic is real | To explain the weather in the morning
